<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 21 L5. THE METRONOME IS A LIVE-LANE SOURCE, and it clicks on the
  beat grid.

  Env, set on the CTest entry (see smaragd/CMakeLists.txt): RUN_SERIAL and
  SMARAGD_CAPTURE_SPEED=1. This is a wall-clock case in exactly the sense the
  L1b/L2 playback cases are - the click is produced by the PUMP and consumed by
  the RT callback, and the MEASUREMENT is the audio capture backend's own
  recording of what the device was handed, which shares no code with either.

  No SMARAGD_AUDIO_INPUT_BACKEND: the metronome has no audio input at all. It
  is a live source that is a pure function of POSITION, which is the whole
  design (twmetronome.h) - so a headless run needs no device on the input side.

  THE CLOSED FORM. A new project is 120 BPM, 4/4, 48 kHz, so

      beat = 48000 * 60 / 120 = 24000 frames
      bar  = 4 * 24000        = 96000 frames = 2 s

  and the accented click (beat 1 of a bar, 2 kHz square) is at the level
  SOpt::MetronomeLevel names while an ordinary beat (1 kHz square) is 0.7 of it
  (twmetronome.h's tone spec) - so the accent ratio is exactly 1/0.7 ~= 1.4286
  by construction, and the 1.3 asserted below is that with room for the onset
  detector's window.

  WHAT IS NOT A CLOSED FORM, and is therefore bounded rather than asserted: HOW
  MANY clicks a wall-clock `wait-ms` produces, and WHERE capture frame 0 falls
  relative to the beat grid. Capture frame 0 is the DEVICE start, and how many
  blocks the ring took to fill before the first entry was summed is a property
  of the box. The SPACING is not - it comes from the tempo map - and that is
  what `intervalFrames` gates, anchored on the first onset. The bar accent's
  PHASE is searched for the same reason.

  ...AND THE FIRST SECOND IS SKIPPED, which is not a convenience. A live lane
  that comes up on a STOPPED->PLAYING transition costs exactly ONE REPOSITION
  (design D2): the pump starts at the locator while the engine clock is still
  invalid, the frozen lane then primes and publishes, and the pump repositions
  onto it - abandoning a run whose entries the consumer drops. MEASURED on this
  box, at workers=1: the beat at frame 0 is delivered EARLY in about one run in
  fifty and swallowed in the other forty-nine, with a ~5087-frame (106 ms) hole
  after it either way. The steady grid after that is exact to five frames.

  So the window starts at 48000 (one second in). Anchoring on a click that may
  or may not be a survivor of the abandoned run would make this case a coin
  flip on the box's timing rather than a gate on the beat grid - it failed
  exactly that way, 49/50, before the window was moved.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="metronome_click">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <!-- One empty track. The project is otherwise silent, so everything in the
         capture below is the click and nothing else. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-tempo bpm="120"/>

    <!-- PHASE A: metronome ON, two bars of transport. ..................... -->
    <metronome-enable/>
    <set-locator position="0"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="30000"/>
    <!-- The lane exists BECAUSE of the metronome: nothing is armed and nothing
         monitors, so `live=on` here is the "armed u monitor u metronome"
         predicate being true on its third term alone. -->
    <assert-input-meter trackPath="0" contains="metronome=on"/>
    <wait-ms ms="4200"/>
    <toggle-playback play="0"/>
    <dump-playback-capture filename="met_on.wav" minFrames="96000"/>

    <!-- From one second in (see the header). Five is the floor the remaining
         3.2 s cannot miss even if the device took a while to start; twelve is
         the ceiling 4.2 s of beats cannot exceed. The claims that MATTER are
         the ones between them. -->
    <assert-metronome-clicks filename="met_on.wav" channel="0"
                             startFrame="48000"
                             threshold="0.05" window="64" minGapFrames="4800"
                             minCount="5" maxCount="12"
                             intervalFrames="24000" toleranceFrames="1024"
                             accentEvery="4" accentRatio="1.3"
                             silenceMaxRms="0.01"/>

    <!-- PHASE B: metronome OFF - a silent project stays silent. ............ -->
    <metronome-disable/>
    <set-locator position="0"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="30000"/>
    <wait-ms ms="2500"/>
    <toggle-playback play="0"/>
    <dump-playback-capture filename="met_off.wav" minFrames="48000"/>
    <assert-metronome-clicks filename="met_off.wav" channel="0"
                             threshold="0.05" window="64" count="0"/>

    <!-- The pump never rendered a page and no freeze met a live-owned
         processor: a metronome lane live-owns NOTHING at all. -->
    <assert-render-policy liveThreadRefusals="0" liveOwnedRefusals="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
